===== FILE: Bits\Designer\ui\PHASE1-README.md =====
# StreamCraft.Forms - Phase 1 Implementation

## ✅ Phase 1 Complete: Core Controls & Event System

Phase 1 of the WinForms-like library implementation is now complete! Five essential input controls have been added along with a robust event system foundation.

### New Controls

#### 1. Label
```xml
<label text="Username:" style="font-weight: bold;" />
```
- Display static text
- Supports text alignment
- Can use `text` prop or inline content

#### 2. TextBox  
```xml
<textBox value="" placeholder="Enter text" onChange="handleChange" />
<textBox value="" multiline="true" rows="5" />
<textBox value="" password="true" />
```
- Single-line or multiline input
- Password masking
- Events: onChange, onFocus, onBlur, onKeyPress
- Properties: placeholder, readOnly, maxLength

#### 3. Button
```xml
<button text="OK" onClick="handleClick" default="true" />
<button text="Cancel" enabled="false" />
```
- Clickable button with onClick event
- Default button support
- Enable/disable state

#### 4. CheckBox
```xml
<checkBox text="Remember me" checked="false" onChange="handleCheck" />
```
- Boolean toggle with label
- onChange event with checked state

#### 5. RadioButton
```xml
<radioButton text="Option A" group="choice" checked="true" />
<radioButton text="Option B" group="choice" />
```
- Exclusive selection within a group
- Group-based mutual exclusion
- onChange event

### Event System

Event handlers are registered in code and referenced by name in XML:

```typescript
const handlers = {
  buttonClick: (args: any) => {
    console.log("Button clicked!", args);
  },
  textChange: (args: any) => {
    console.log("Text changed:", args.value);
  }
};

<FormContainer node={formNode} handlers={handlers} />
```

### Try It Now!

1. **Start the app**: `.\runlocal.ps1 -watch`
2. **Open browser console**
3. **Run**: `window.debug.sc.testForm()`

This will open a fully functional test form showcasing all five controls with live event handling.

### Architecture

- **Control files**: `Bits/Designer/ui/src/forms/controls/*Control.tsx`
- **Event system**: `FormContainer.tsx` wraps controls and provides event context
- **Registration**: Controls registered in `controls/index.ts`
- **Types**: Extended `ControlContext` with `eventHandlers` and `raiseEvent`
- **Styling**: Basic CSS in `controls/controls.css`

### Next Phase: Layout Containers

Phase 2 will implement:
- FlowLayoutPanel (horizontal/vertical auto-flow)
- TableLayoutPanel (grid-based layout)
- Dock property system (Top, Bottom, Left, Right, Fill)
- Anchor property system (responsive edge anchoring)

See [impl.details.md](impl.details.md) for the complete implementation roadmap.



===== FILE: Bits\Designer\ui\PLAYGROUND-GUIDE.md =====
# Control Playground Guide

## Launch the Playground

Open your browser console and run:
```javascript
window.debug.sc.playground()
```

## What's Inside

The Playground showcases **all 5 Phase 1 controls** with **40+ variants and combinations**:

### 1. Labels (7 variants)
- Default, Bold, Colored (success/error), Large
- Text alignment: Left, Center, Right

### 2. TextBoxes (9 variants)
- Single-line with placeholder
- Password masking
- Read-only
- Event handling (onChange, onFocus, onBlur, onKeyPress)
- Multiline (3 rows and 8 rows)
- MaxLength constraint

### 3. Buttons (12+ variants)
- Standard, Default (bold), Disabled
- With icon text (✓ ✗ ⟲ ⚙)
- Various sizes (Small, Normal, Large)

### 4. CheckBoxes (8 variants)
- Checked/Unchecked states
- Enabled/Disabled states
- Independent groups

### 5. RadioButtons (8 variants)
- Multiple independent groups
- Disabled states
- Mutual exclusion within groups

### Complete Form Example
Full user registration form demonstrating:
- Grid layout with multiple fields
- Mixed control types
- Form submission/cancellation
- Real-world usage patterns

## Features Demonstrated

✅ **Styling** - Colors, fonts, sizes, alignment  
✅ **States** - Enabled/disabled, checked/unchecked  
✅ **Events** - All controls log events to console  
✅ **Layout** - Flexbox, grid, responsive  
✅ **Validation** - MaxLength, password masking, read-only  
✅ **Grouping** - Radio groups, fieldsets  
✅ **Composition** - Complex multi-control forms

## Usage Tips

1. **Watch the console** - All events are logged
2. **Try interactions** - Click, type, focus, blur
3. **Test states** - Toggle checkboxes, select radios
4. **Explore styling** - Notice colors, fonts, sizes
5. **Check responsiveness** - Resize multiline textboxes

## Next: Phase 2

Coming soon:
- FlowLayoutPanel (auto-flow layouts)
- TableLayoutPanel (grid layouts)
- Dock properties (Top, Bottom, Left, Right, Fill)
- Anchor properties (edge anchoring)

See [impl.details.md](../../impl.details.md) for the complete roadmap.



