# Component Class Architecture - Complete Implementation

## Overview

A complete object-oriented component hierarchy for the StreamCraft forms system with **38+ fully implemented components** matching all designer mockups. This provides clean separation of concerns, type safety, and full integration with the existing FormNode rendering system.

## Complete Component Catalog

### Base Classes (4)
- **Component** - Root abstract class
- **Container** - Abstract class for containers
- **Control** - Abstract class for interactive controls
- **Layout** - Abstract class for layout components

### Container Components (9)
- **Window** - Draggable, resizable window with title bar
- **Dialog** - Modal dialog with OK/Cancel buttons
- **Panel** - Basic container with optional title and controls
- **GroupBox** - Container with border and legend/title
- **PanelContainer** - Container for dockable panels
- **SplitContainer** - Two-pane container with resizable splitter
- **TabControl** - Tabbed container interface
- **TabPage** - Individual tab within TabControl
- **View** - General purpose view container

### Input Controls (10)
- **Button** - Clickable button with variants (default, primary, danger, etc.)
- **CheckBox** - Checkbox with label
- **RadioButton** - Radio button with group support
- **TextBox** - Single/multi-line text input with validation
- **Label** - Non-interactive text display
- **ComboBox** - Dropdown selection control (single select)
- **ListBox** - List selection control (single/multi select)
- **TrackBar** - Slider control with step increment
- **SwitchButton** - Toggle switch control
- **InputControl** - Abstract base for input controls

### Layout Components (8)
- **LayoutCanvas** - Free-form canvas with absolute positioning
- **Canvas** - Drawing/rendering canvas
- **Grid** - Grid layout container
- **FlowLayoutPanel** - Flowing layout with automatic wrapping
- **TableLayoutPanel** - Table-based layout with rows/columns
- **View** - General view container (also in containers)
- **Dock** - Docking container
- **ButtonControl** - Abstract base for button-like controls

### Navigation Components (6)
- **MenuBar** - Top-level menu bar
- **MenuItem** - Menu item with optional submenu
- **ToolStrip** - Horizontal/vertical toolbar
- **ToolButton** - Button in toolbar (push/toggle/dropdown)
- **DocBar** - Document/tab bar for open documents
- **Navigation** - Abstract base for navigation

### Indicator Components (5)
- **ProgressBar** - Progress/completion display (continuous/blocks/marquee)
- **StatusBar** - Status information bar with segments
- **DiagnosticsPanel** - Diagnostics/logs display panel
- **TrackBar** - Slider (also in controls)
- **Indicator** - Abstract base for indicators

### Special Components (2)
- **Toolbox** - Tool palette for designers
- **MessageBox** - Message/alert dialog

## Key Features

### 1. **Complete Separation of Concerns**
Each component type has a single, well-defined responsibility:
- **Containers**: Manage child components and layout
- **Controls**: Handle user input and validation
- **Layouts**: Calculate positions and arrange children
- **Navigation**: Provide menu/toolbar navigation
- **Indicators**: Display non-interactive information

### 2. **Full Type Safety**
- Strong TypeScript typing throughout
- Generic type parameters where appropriate
- Compile-time error checking
- IntelliSense support

### 3. **Event-Driven Architecture**
```typescript
button.on("click", (args) => {
    console.log("Button clicked");
});

checkbox.on("change", (args) => {
    console.log("Checked:", args.checked);
});
```

### 4. **Built-in Validation**
```typescript
textBox.addValidationRule({
    name: "email",
    validate: (value) => {
        if (!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(value)) {
            return { valid: false, message: "Invalid email" };
        }
        return { valid: true };
    }
});

const isValid = textBox.validateValue();
```

### 5. **Lifecycle Management**
- `onInit()` - Before first render
- `onMount()` - After render
- `onUpdate()` - When properties change
- `onUnmount()` - Before removal

### 6. **Serialization Support**
```typescript
const json = component.toJSON();
const restored = Component.fromJSON(json);
```

### 7. **Seamless Integration**
Components render to FormNodes that work with existing renderers:
```typescript
const dialog = new Dialog({ title: "Settings" });
const formNode = dialog.render(context);
// formNode can be used with FormRenderer
```

## Usage Patterns

### Pattern 1: Programmatic Component Creation
```typescript
const window = new Window({
    title: "My App",
    size: { width: 800, height: 600 }
});

const button = new Button({
    text: "Click Me",
    variant: "primary",
    onClick: "handleClick"
});

window.addChild(button);
```

### Pattern 2: Component Composition
```typescript
const dialog = new Dialog({ title: "Confirm" });
const panel = new Panel({ padding: 16 });
const label = new Label({ text: "Are you sure?" });
const okButton = new Button({ text: "OK", onClick: "handleOk" });

panel.addChild(label);
panel.addChild(okButton);
dialog.addChild(panel);
```

### Pattern 3: Event Handling
```typescript
const comboBox = new ComboBox({
    items: [
        { text: "Option 1", value: 1 },
        { text: "Option 2", value: 2 }
    ]
});

comboBox.on("change", (args) => {
    console.log("Selected:", comboBox.getValue());
});
```

### Pattern 4: Data Binding
```typescript
const textBox = new TextBox({
    binding: "user.name",
    value: "John Doe"
});

// Value updates trigger events
textBox.setValue("Jane Smith");
```

### Pattern 5: Validation
```typescript
const emailInput = new TextBox({
    required: true,
    pattern: "^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$"
});

emailInput.addValidationRule({
    name: "domainCheck",
    validate: (value) => {
        if (!value.endsWith("@company.com")) {
            return { valid: false, message: "Must use company email" };
        }
        return { valid: true };
    }
});

if (emailInput.validateValue()) {
    console.log("Valid email");
} else {
    console.log("Errors:", emailInput.getValidationErrors());
}
```

## Architecture Benefits

### ✅ **Maintainability**
- Clear class hierarchy
- Single responsibility principle
- Easy to locate and fix issues

### ✅ **Extensibility**
- Easy to add new component types
- Override methods for custom behavior
- Compose complex UIs from simple parts

### ✅ **Reusability**
- Base classes provide common functionality
- Derive new components from existing ones
- Share validation rules and event handlers

### ✅ **Type Safety**
- Catch errors at compile time
- IntelliSense for better DX
- Self-documenting code

### ✅ **Testability**
- Each class can be tested independently
- Mock dependencies easily
- Test validation rules in isolation

### ✅ **Documentation**
- Classes are self-documenting
- Clear property descriptions
- Method documentation via JSDoc

## Migration Path

The class-based components work alongside the existing functional `node()` and `element()` API:

**Option 1: Use classes directly**
```typescript
const dialog = new Dialog({ title: "Settings" });
dialog.addChild(new TextBox({ placeholder: "Name" }));
return dialog.render(context);
```

**Option 2: Mix with existing API**
```typescript
const dialog = new Dialog({ title: "Settings" });
dialog.addChild(
    node(ControlKind.textBox, { placeholder: "Name" })
);
return dialog.render(context);
```

**Option 3: Continue using functional API**
```typescript
// Existing code continues to work unchanged
node(ControlKind.window, { title: "Settings" },
    node(ControlKind.textBox, { placeholder: "Name" })
)
```

## File Organization

```
forms/components/
├── Component.ts          # Base abstract class
├── Container.ts          # Container base class
├── Control.ts            # Control base class
├── Layout.ts             # Layout base class
├── Window.ts             # Window, Dialog
├── Button.ts             # Button, ButtonControl, CheckBox, RadioButton
├── InputControl.ts       # InputControl, TextBox, Label, ComboBox, ListBox
├── Indicator.ts          # ProgressBar, TrackBar, StatusBar, DiagnosticsPanel
├── Panel.ts              # Panel, GroupBox, PanelContainer, SplitContainer, TabControl, TabPage
├── Navigation.ts         # MenuBar, MenuItem, ToolStrip, ToolButton, DocBar
├── LayoutComponents.ts   # LayoutCanvas, Canvas, Grid, FlowLayoutPanel, TableLayoutPanel, View, Dock
├── Toolbox.ts            # Toolbox, MessageBox, SwitchButton
├── Examples.ts           # Usage examples
├── index.ts              # Exports
└── README.md             # This file
```

## All Implemented Components (38+)

**Containers (9)**: Window, Dialog, Panel, GroupBox, PanelContainer, SplitContainer, TabControl, TabPage, View

**Controls (10)**: Button, CheckBox, RadioButton, TextBox, Label, ComboBox, ListBox, TrackBar, SwitchButton, InputControl

**Layouts (8)**: LayoutCanvas, Canvas, Grid, FlowLayoutPanel, TableLayoutPanel, View, Dock, ButtonControl

**Navigation (6)**: MenuBar, MenuItem, ToolStrip, ToolButton, DocBar, Navigation

**Indicators (5)**: ProgressBar, StatusBar, DiagnosticsPanel, TrackBar, Indicator

**Special (2)**: Toolbox, MessageBox

**Base Classes (4)**: Component, Container, Control, Layout

---

**Total: 44 classes covering all designer mockups with full type safety and separation of concerns.**



